# TEST-only tools for the sidecar's unit and HTTP-contract tests, installed
# into a throwaway environment -- never into the shipped image.
#
# fastapi and python-multipart are the HTTP layer's own runtime deps
# (starlette comes with fastapi). They are listed UNPINNED: their versions
# come from requirements.in through the constraint below (requirements.in now
# pins every top-level package by exact version, #1017, so it is a valid
# constraint source on its own -- there is no longer a single portable
# requirements.txt to point at, since the runtime lock is per-architecture,
# see requirements-linux-amd64.txt / requirements-linux-arm64.txt), so this
# lock cannot drift from the runtime pin. A constraint only pins what is
# requested, so torch/demucs/faster-whisper never enter this lock and the
# test venv stays ML-free. Regenerate with uv (the recipe in
# requirements-test.txt): pip/pip-tools refuse this constraint file
# ("Constraints cannot have extras", from uvicorn[standard]).
#
# httpx is not a direct import of test_app.py -- it is what
# starlette.testclient.TestClient requires, and the concurrency tests use
# httpx.ASGITransport directly.
-c requirements.in
pytest
httpx
fastapi
python-multipart
